learnings[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T14:58:03.382Z","harness:codex",Entity read projection must derive its selectable top-level vocabulary from the actual result envelope while keeping item-field vocabulary stable; otherwise a selector either lies about absent data or silently disappears.
  "2026-08-07T15:48:49.314Z","harness:codex",Projection conflicts should name the exact entity and depth pair so an agent can repair the selector without translating generic section terminology.
  "2026-08-07T16:35:53.348Z","harness:codex","A projection receipt is additive context, not a replacement envelope: every shaping layer must preserve upstream omission disclosures and recompute aggregate truth from the combined groups."
  "2026-08-26T22:51:36.521Z","harness:codex",Canonical collection selection must be forwarded before command execution and then mirrored into the CLI parser; shaping only after execution cannot recover collections omitted by the SDK read contract.
